      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.31,
          "end": 5.08,
          "en": "So, I am back in this project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.08,
          "end": 6.93,
          "en": "we set up in the last module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.93,
          "end": 8.3,
          "en": "you'll find it attached,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.3,
          "end": 10.2,
          "en": "make sure to run NPM install",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.2,
          "end": 11.41,
          "en": "and start your server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 11.41,
          "end": 14.043,
          "en": "with NPM run server if you just downloaded it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.47,
          "end": 17.55,
          "en": "And you should see this on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.55,
          "end": 20.39,
          "en": "on localhost 8080 here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.39,
          "end": 24.49,
          "en": "So, this is the dummy application we work thus far,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.49,
          "end": 26.72,
          "en": "and we're using a component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.72,
          "end": 29.44,
          "en": "we're using the friend contact component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.44,
          "end": 33.223,
          "en": "which we define here in main JS with app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.2,
          "end": 38.88,
          "en": "Now this friend contact component has one problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.88,
          "end": 40.68,
          "en": "it has one flaw.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.68,
          "end": 42.75,
          "en": "The data which we're outputting here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.75,
          "end": 44.35,
          "en": "the name of the friend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.35,
          "end": 46.73,
          "en": "the phone number, the email address,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.73,
          "end": 51.19,
          "en": "all of that is stored here inside of the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.19,
          "end": 54.01,
          "en": "in this friend data property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.01,
          "end": 56.96,
          "en": "Now, that's a pattern we used a lot throughout this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.96,
          "end": 59.96,
          "en": "We stored the data a Vue app needs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.96,
          "end": 61.8,
          "en": "inside of that app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 61.8,
          "end": 64.9,
          "en": "But for components, it often is a bit different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 64.9,
          "end": 69.39,
          "en": "There, you sometimes want to create a reusable component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.39,
          "end": 72.76,
          "en": "which contains the markup and certain logic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.76,
          "end": 75.86,
          "en": "like here, the logic for toggling the list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.86,
          "end": 77.07,
          "en": "with help of the button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 77.07,
          "end": 79.76,
          "en": "so that should be part of the component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 79.76,
          "end": 83.41,
          "en": "But some data should be received from outside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.41,
          "end": 87.62,
          "en": "and with from outside I mean that the app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.62,
          "end": 90.69,
          "en": "or component which is using this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.69,
          "end": 93.25,
          "en": "so in our case, our main app here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.25,
          "end": 95.81,
          "en": "here, where we are using that component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 95.81,
          "end": 100.53,
          "en": "that app here should pass data into our component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.53,
          "end": 103.68,
          "en": "so that when we use our component twice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 103.68,
          "end": 106.2,
          "en": "we can use it with different data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.2,
          "end": 108.41,
          "en": "in each component instance,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 108.41,
          "end": 111.68299999999999,
          "en": "so in each HTML element we're creating here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 112.61,
          "end": 116.74000000000001,
          "en": "So that the first contact outputs the data about manual",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 116.74000000000001,
          "end": 119.28999999999999,
          "en": "and the second time we use the component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 119.28999999999999,
          "end": 122.5,
          "en": "we for example, output data about Julie.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 122.5,
          "end": 123.84,
          "en": "That would be great",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 123.84,
          "end": 126.34,
          "en": "if we could use a component like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 126.34,
          "end": 129.4,
          "en": "if we could use it as a reusable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 129.4,
          "end": 132.5,
          "en": "and configurable HTML element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 132.5,
          "end": 135.49,
          "en": "And at the moment it's kind of reusable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 135.49,
          "end": 138.34,
          "en": "but every usage contains the same data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 138.34,
          "end": 140.963,
          "en": "which is why we see Manuel Lorenz twice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 141.93,
          "end": 144.89,
          "en": "Now of course, there is a solution for this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 144.89,
          "end": 148.04,
          "en": "because this is such a crucial concept,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 148.04,
          "end": 151.64,
          "en": "being able to configure the same component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 151.64,
          "end": 152.88,
          "en": "with different data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 152.88,
          "end": 154.57999999999998,
          "en": "when you use it multiple times,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 154.57999999999998,
          "end": 156.35,
          "en": "that is a core concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 156.35,
          "end": 159.92000000000002,
          "en": "and therefore it is something we can implement with Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 159.92000000000002,
          "end": 162.78,
          "en": "with a concept called props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 162.78,
          "end": 165.12,
          "en": "Now what are props about?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 165.12,
          "end": 168.49,
          "en": "Props is short for properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 168.49,
          "end": 173.32999999999998,
          "en": "and you can think of props like custom HTML attributes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 173.32999999999998,
          "end": 176.79,
          "en": "For example here, in App.vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 176.79,
          "end": 179.47,
          "en": "it would be nice if we could pass data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 179.47,
          "end": 181.37,
          "en": "to our first friend contact.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 181.37,
          "end": 185.79,
          "en": "Let's say we would pass in the name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 185.79,
          "end": 188.14,
          "en": "and that would be Manuel Lorenz.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 188.14,
          "end": 191.81,
          "en": "We would pass in the phone number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 191.81,
          "end": 194.783,
          "en": "and that would be some number here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 195.69,
          "end": 199.3,
          "en": "And we would pass in the email address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 199.3,
          "end": 204.3,
          "en": "and that would be manuel@localhost.com for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 204.76,
          "end": 207.56,
          "en": "And I'm going to hit that reformat shortcut",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 207.56,
          "end": 211.8,
          "en": "to reformat it into this more readable version here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 211.8,
          "end": 212.84,
          "en": "But it would be nice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 212.84,
          "end": 217.23,
          "en": "if we could use our friend contact component like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 217.23,
          "end": 221.06,
          "en": "And then here for the second friend contact component usage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 221.06,
          "end": 223.91,
          "en": "we could pass in the same attributes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 223.91,
          "end": 225.8,
          "en": "but with different data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 225.8,
          "end": 228.82999999999998,
          "en": "So we could copy that and add it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 228.82999999999998,
          "end": 231.67000000000002,
          "en": "but now on that second friend contact,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 231.67000000000002,
          "end": 234.36,
          "en": "pass in Julie Jones,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 234.36,
          "end": 239.36,
          "en": "with some data of our choice here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 240.63,
          "end": 242.77,
          "en": "and hear julie@localhost.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 242.77,
          "end": 245.113,
          "en": "It would be nice if we could use it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 246.97,
          "end": 248.92,
          "en": "Now, if we save that it works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 248.92,
          "end": 251.82,
          "en": "but of course we don't see that data on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 251.82,
          "end": 253.43,
          "en": "Because, yes, indeed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 253.43,
          "end": 256.1,
          "en": "you can set your own attributes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 256.1,
          "end": 259.89,
          "en": "those so called props on components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 259.89,
          "end": 262.63,
          "en": "but in order to use them inside of the component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 262.63,
          "end": 264.44,
          "en": "you also need to write some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 264.44,
          "end": 266.2,
          "en": "inside of the component file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 266.2,
          "end": 269.39300000000003,
          "en": "so in this case, inside of friend contact.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 270.3,
          "end": 275.067,
          "en": "You basically should make Vue aware of the attributes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 275.067,
          "end": 279.123,
          "en": "of the props that you want to accept on your component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 280.64,
          "end": 281.92,
          "en": "So in our case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 281.92,
          "end": 284.45,
          "en": "we want to make Vue aware of name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 284.45,
          "end": 288.5,
          "en": "of phone number and of email address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 288.5,
          "end": 290.82,
          "en": "And we can make Vue aware of this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 290.82,
          "end": 293.27,
          "en": "by going to our component file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 293.27,
          "end": 295.07,
          "en": "into the config object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 295.07,
          "end": 298.39,
          "en": "and by adding a specific new key here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 298.39,
          "end": 301.61,
          "en": "a new property which we haven't learned about before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 301.61,
          "end": 303.92,
          "en": "the props property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 303.92,
          "end": 307.75,
          "en": "And in its simplest form, this takes an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 307.75,
          "end": 310.09,
          "en": "I'm saying in its simplest form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 310.09,
          "end": 312.98,
          "en": "because we will later also learn about different ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 312.98,
          "end": 314.64,
          "en": "of using that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 314.64,
          "end": 318.05,
          "en": "But in the simplest form, we pass in an array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 318.05,
          "end": 322.61,
          "en": "and in here, we should now specify all the props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 322.61,
          "end": 325.41,
          "en": "So, all the custom attributes, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 325.41,
          "end": 329.25,
          "en": "we want to accept on this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 329.25,
          "end": 331.22,
          "en": "And in our case, that would be name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 331.22,
          "end": 333.61,
          "en": "phone number and email address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 333.61,
          "end": 336.77,
          "en": "So we could add name, as a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 336.77,
          "end": 339.9,
          "en": "you add your props as strings to this array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 339.9,
          "end": 341.84000000000003,
          "en": "So we add name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 341.84000000000003,
          "end": 345.31,
          "en": "and then phone number, written like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 345.31,
          "end": 347.1,
          "en": "I'll come back to that in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 347.1,
          "end": 350.02,
          "en": "And email address also written like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 350.02,
          "end": 351.63,
          "en": "Now why is phone number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 351.63,
          "end": 353.92,
          "en": "and email address written like this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 353.92,
          "end": 358.13,
          "en": "Because, what we define here as props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 358.13,
          "end": 361.49,
          "en": "will be available, just like data properties,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 361.49,
          "end": 363.38,
          "en": "in this entire Vue component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 363.38,
          "end": 365.7,
          "en": "including in the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 365.7,
          "end": 368.11,
          "en": "So, we could now refer to this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 368.11,
          "end": 369.66,
          "en": "with the \"this\" keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 369.66,
          "end": 371.69,
          "en": "Here in the method if we needed it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 371.69,
          "end": 376.69,
          "en": "we could refer to this phone number for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 376.75,
          "end": 378.45,
          "en": "And that's why we write it like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 378.45,
          "end": 379.89,
          "en": "and not with a dash,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 379.89,
          "end": 381.03,
          "en": "because with a dash,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 381.03,
          "end": 384.36,
          "en": "this would be an invalid JavaScript property name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 384.36,
          "end": 386.8,
          "en": "this would be invalid JavaScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 386.8,
          "end": 389.48,
          "en": "And therefore props in your component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 389.48,
          "end": 392.52,
          "en": "should be defined in this camel case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 392.52,
          "end": 397.52,
          "en": "And Vue automatically translates props defined like this",
